Example data files used by dbparser's examples, tests and vignettes
==================================================================

hgnc/
-----
hgnc_complete_set.txt and withdrawn.txt are small extracts of the HUGO Gene
Nomenclature Committee (HGNC) files of the same names, downloaded on
2026-10-16 from https://www.genenames.org/download/statistics-and-files/.

- hgnc_complete_set.txt: the header line and the unchanged lines of 24 genes
  (PDCD1, SNCA, SPATA2, HACD1, LNPEP, BRD4, SERPINB6, CAP1, SORBS1, CD274,
  SEPTIN1, MARCHF1, ERBB2, CTLA4, F11, TP53, RBFOX1, RUVBL1, ACTB, AURKA,
  LINC00595, LINC00856, OPN1MW, OPN1LW).
- withdrawn.txt: the header line and the unchanged lines of 7 withdrawn
  entries (HGNC:1, HGNC:2, HGNC:231, HGNC:1531, HGNC:12797, HGNC:21128,
  HGNC:7810).

Licence: HGNC data are released under the Creative Commons Public Domain
(CC0) licence, https://www.genenames.org/about/license/. HGNC recommends
citing:

  Seal RL, Braschi B, Gray K, McClay J, Tweedie S, Bruford EA.
  Genenames.org: the HGNC and PGNC resources in 2026. Nucleic Acids Research
  (Database issue). HGNC (RRID:SCR_002827).

health_canada_dpd/
------------------
Small extracts of Health Canada's Drug Product Database (DPD) data extract,
downloaded on 2026-10-21 from
https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/drugs-health-products/drug-products/drug-product-database/what-data-extract-drug-product-database.html

The unchanged lines (comma-separated, quoted, no header, CRLF, UTF-8) of 12
products: marketed 15, 85, 129, 18349, 81048; approved 14535, 99581;
cancelled 2, 80771, 94947; dormant 31, 126. Each set keeps its file names:
allfiles/ (marketed), allfiles_ap/ (approved), allfiles_ia/ (cancelled, with
its copy of inactive.txt), allfiles_dr.zip (dormant, kept zipped to exercise
reading from a zip) and inactive/inactive.txt. Files with no row for these
products are empty, as biosimilar_dr.txt is in the full extract.

Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada.
Licence: Open Government Licence – Canada, version 2.0,
https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada
Dataset record: "Drug Product Database - All Files",
https://open.canada.ca/data/en/dataset/bf55e42a-63cb-4556-bfd8-44f26e5a36fe
The DPD extract page also links to Health Canada's website terms; the
dataset record on open.canada.ca states the Open Government Licence –
Canada.
